<title>SWITZERLAND: Selecta IPO indicated 180-212 Sfr.</title>
<headline>Selecta IPO indicated 180-212 Sfr.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss retail group Valora Holding AG and Union Bank of Switzerland said that the price on an initial public offering of shares in Selecta was set in a range from 180 to 212 Swiss francs per registered share.</p>
<p>The subsription period ends May 9. The final share price will be set on May 12.</p>
<p>The shares will be listed in Switzerland and in London.</p>
<p>After the IPO, up to 60 percent of Selecta's capital will be in public hands, and the remainder will be retained by Valora and the U.K.-based Compass Group.</p>
<p>Selecta specialises in vending machine sales.</p>
<p>Valora's business is concentrated in kiosks, speciality shops and bedding stores.</p>
<p>Valora changed its name last year from Merkur Holding.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
